  "notes": [
    "Weigh boneless meat for the 4 lb. Bone-in short ribs and oxtail yield less meat per pound, so add more. Mixing cuts is fine: use the longest time.",
    "Don’t braise the steaks (sirloin, T-bone, hanger, tri-tip) or cubed or round steak. They go dry and stringy.",
    "Skimmed pot-roast liquid can stand in for some or all of the stock.",
    "Store leftovers in the juices and reheat in a skillet. Good for burrito bowls or crispy quesadillas."
